LAYERED LICENSING NOTICE
========================

This project is open source under a layered policy. Each layer has its own
license file in the repository root; the policy is also specified as the
`licensing` capability in openspec/specs/licensing/spec.md.

LAYER 1 — SPECS, RESEARCH AND DOCUMENTATION
    Files: openspec/**, BLUEPRINT.md, OPENSPEC.md, *.md documentation
    License: CC BY-SA 4.0 (SPDX: CC-BY-SA-4.0)
    Full text: LICENSE-CONTENT.txt
    Canonical: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/legalcode.txt

LAYER 2 — GAME CODE (engine, backend, frontend, tools, tests)
    Files: backend/**, frontend/**, tools/**, and any source code
    License: AGPL-3.0-or-later (SPDX: AGPL-3.0-or-later)
    Full text: LICENSE-CODE.txt
    Canonical: https://www.gnu.org/licenses/agpl-3.0.txt
    Note: AGPL-3.0 is one-way compatible with the GPL-3.0 of the d3wasm
    engine (Doom 3 / id Tech 4 in WebAssembly) considered by the engine
    path — GPL-3.0 code may be incorporated into AGPL-3.0 works, and the
    AGPL's network clause (section 13) carries over. This closes the
    SaaS/network-service loophole: anyone operating a modified server
    must publish the modifications.

LAYER 3 — GAME CANON AND CONTENT
    Files: scenarios, story cards, lore, the "O Cidadão do Futuro"
    universe and all authored game content
    License: CC BY-SA 4.0 (SPDX: CC-BY-SA-4.0)
    Full text: LICENSE-CONTENT.txt
    Rationale: share-alike enforces the architecture specified in
    mmo-game — cultural shards as configuration over shared canon,
    never forked lore. Derivatives must share alike.

LAYER 4 — TRADEMARK AND BRAND
    The names "Our Civilization The Game", "Project Lunar" and project
    identity marks are NOT licensed under the above terms; all rights
    reserved by the copyright holder. In a world of community shards,
    the brand is the signal of the official service.

OUT OF LICENSING SCOPE
    Civilization-lab datasets, consent records, research-partnership
    agreements and ethics-board documents are governance artifacts,
    not open-source material; they are governed by their own terms.

CONTRIBUTIONS
    Accepted under the Developer Certificate of Origin (DCO) —
    sign-off git commits (`git commit -s`). The DCO preserves the
    project's flexibility to relicense code layers in the future.

Unless otherwise stated inside a file, the layered policy above applies.
